                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_connectedness"} Relation to connectedness
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#over_"}
                    Over
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#StrongAdjunctions"} Strong adjunctions
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#coreflectivity"} Coreflectivity
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#other_characterizations"} Other characterizations
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#variations_in_the_context_of_the_nullstellensatz"} Variations in the context of the Nullstellensatz
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_entries"} Related entries
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            is
            %em locally connected
            if it behaves as though its
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+space"} locally connected space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected
            iff the unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            (the terminal Grothendieck topos, i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            of toposes) is locally connected.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⇆
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* \dashv f_*) : F \underoverset{f_*}{f^*}{\leftrightarrows} E
            is
            %strong locally connected
            if it satisfies the following equivalent conditions:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                It is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
                can be made into an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+functor"} indexed functor
            %li
              %p
                For every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/A)^* \colon E/A \to F/f^*A
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"} cartesian closed
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
                commutes with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+products"} dependent products
                – For any morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon A\to B
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi B
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mi h
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/B)^* \circ \Pi_h \to \Pi_{f^*h} \circ (f/A)^*
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_connectedness Relation to connectedness
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is locally connected, then it makes sense to think of the left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            as assigning to an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            its “set of connected components” in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is locally connected, then it is moreover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+geometric+morphism"} connected
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            preserves the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %h3#over_
            Over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            Over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected topos
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential
            is automatically locally connected.
          %p
            This is because the required
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            condition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_!(A \times f^* (B)) \simeq f_!(A) \times B
          %p
            is automatically satisfied, using that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \times B = \coprod_{a \in A} B
                  \\,,
          %p
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            preserves coproducts, and that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful"} full and faithful
            we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! f^* \simeq Id
          %h3#StrongAdjunctions Strong adjunctions
          %p
            The pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_! \dashv f^*)
            in a locally connected geometric morphisms forms a “strong adjunction” in that it holds also for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+homs"} internal homs
            in the sense that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [f_!(X), A] \simeq f_* [X, f^* A]
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            that characterizes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            as being a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"} cartesian closed functor
          %p
            by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            if for all objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B, X
            the morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom(X, [f_!(A), B])
                  \\stackrel{}{\to}
                  Hom(X,f_*[A,f^*(B)])
          %p
            is a bijection. By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            this is the same as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom(X \times f_!(A), B) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  Hom(f_!(f^*(X) \times A), B)
                  \\,.
          %p Again by Yoneda, this is a bijection precisely if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_!(f^*(X) \times A) \to X \times f_!(A)
          %p
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            condition on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
          %h3#coreflectivity Coreflectivity
          %p
            Locally connected toposes are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Funk"} Funk (1999)
          %h3#other_characterizations Other characterizations
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, J)
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
                on the object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is called
                %em connected
                when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                viewed as a full subcategory of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}/U
                is connected. The
                %strong site
                is called
                %em locally connected
                if every sieve is connected. For a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+geometric+morphism"} bounded geometric morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{S}
                the following holds:
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is locally connected iff there exists a locally connected internal site in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒮
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
                  such that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo ,
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\simeq Sh(\mathcal{C},J)
                (cf.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#elephant"} Johnstone (2002)
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Cara12"} Caramello (2012)
                gives syntactic characterizations of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theories"} geometric theories
                whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
                is locally connected.
          %p The same paper also contains the following characterization:
          %ul
            %li
              A Grothendieck topos is locally connected iff it has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separating set
              of (coproduct) indecomposable objects.
          %h3#variations_in_the_context_of_the_nullstellensatz Variations in the context of the Nullstellensatz
          %p
            %a{:href => "#JS11"} Johnstone (2011)
            studies several subclasses of locally connected geometric morphisms in the context of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} Lawvere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nullstellensatz"} Nullstellensatz
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %em stably locally connected
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
            preserves finite products. According to the
            %a{:href => "#connect"} above remark
            this implies that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is connected. Slightly stronger is the preservation of all finite limits by
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            are called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+connected+geometric+morphisms"} totally connected geometric morphisms
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If the terminal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
                geometric morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Set
                is locally connected, one calls
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to S
                is locally connected, we may call
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    locally connected
                    = succeed "-topos" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                (or a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X
                an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\colon Sh(U)\to Sh(X)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Sh(X)
                can be identified with a space (or locale)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                equipped with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+homeomorphism"} local homeomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)/A \simeq Sh(A)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*A \in Sh(U)
                can be identified with the pullback of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to X
                along
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(U)/j^*A \simeq Sh(j^*A)
                similarly. Noting that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*A \to A
                is again the inclusion of an open subset, and using the fact that the inverse image part of any open
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
                is cartesian closed, we see that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j/A)^*\colon Sh(X)/A \to Sh(U)/j^*A
                is cartesian closed for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                is locally connected.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+geometric+morphism"} connected geometric morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+geometric+morphism"} local geometric morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+connected+geometric+morphism"} totally connected geometric morphism
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The case of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
            for a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            was an exercise (p.417) in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA4"} SGA4
          %ul
            %li#SGA4
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Artin"}> M. Artin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Grothendieck"} A. Grothendieck
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+L.+Verdier"} J. L. Verdier
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Théorie des Topos et Cohomologie Etale des Schémas (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA4"}> SGA4
                  )
          %p The concept relative to other bases was introduced in the following paper:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"} Robert Paré
              %em Molecular Toposes
              , JPAA
              %strong 17
              (1980) pp.127-152.
          %p The standard reference is section C3.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
              , Oxford UP 2002.
          %p Further references include
          %ul
            %li
              %p#Cara12
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"}> Olivia Caramello
                ,
                %em Syntactic Characterizations of Properties of Classifying Toposes
                , TAC
                %strong 26
                no.6 (2012) pp.176-193. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/6/26-06.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p#Funk
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathon+Funk"}> Jonathon Funk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The locally connected coclosure of a Grothendieck topos
                %strong 137
                (1999) pp.17-27.
            %li#JS11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em Remarks on Punctual Local Connectedness
                , TAC
                %strong 25
                no.3 (2011) pp.51-63. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/25/3/25-03abs.html"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                %em Continuous fibrations and inverse limits of toposes
                , Comp. Math.
                %strong 58
                (1986) pp.45-72. (
                %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/article/CM_1986__58_1_45_0.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Wraith"} Gavin Wraith
                %em Connected and locally connected toposes are path connected
                , Trans. AMS
                %strong 295
                (1986) pp.849-859. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/tran/1986-295-02/S0002-9947-1986-0833712-3/S0002-9947-1986-0833712-3.pdf"}> pdf
                )
